# Git commit author

When creating git commits (including empty redeploy commits), always set author and committer via environment variables for that command only — do **not** run `git config`:

- Name: `yerandyalfonso`
- Email: `yerandy.alfonso@gmail.com`

Example:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="yerandyalfonso" \
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="yerandy.alfonso@gmail.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="yerandyalfonso" \
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="yerandy.alfonso@gmail.com" \
git commit ...
```

This email must match the GitHub account so Vercel does not block deployments.
